      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-26T18:36:44Z",
      "note": "The Safe was created by factory 0xa6b71e26c5e0845f74c812102ca7114b6a896ab2 at block 16132578:90. Safe v1.3.0 source places the singleton in slot 0. Transaction 0x48164d3adbab78c2cb9876f6e17f88e321097fcd14cadd57556866e4ef3e185d at block 20331565:21 delegatecalled helper 0xfbffef83b1c172fe3bc86c1ccb036ab9f3efcaf2 and changed that slot from 0xd9db270c1b5e3bd161e8c8503c55ceabee709552 to 0xef279c2ab14960aa319008cbea384b9f8ac35fc6. The latter was deployed at block 20274652:174 and its runtime hashes to 0x032920c4cf440ec3fe6d4e40ea5e9006387b1be67adf3393c2b12d3e2094800b both there and in the anchor prestate. The first later call to its 0x2d8a122e drain function is the anchor at block 20331573:46; its trace delegatecalls the declared singleton and transfers 4.104646231600560442 GNO to 0x04b21735e93fa3f8df70e2da89e6922616891a88. An Etherscan account scan found 203 successful attacker calls after the reset, ending with source-2's final transaction. Before the ETH drain at block 20331578:25, the Safe held exactly 15,298.162196710885193018 ETH; afterward it held zero and the trace sends that amount to the same receiver. Chainlink feed 0x5f4ec3df9cbd43714fe2740f5e3616155c5b8419 returned 342954425473 with 8 decimals and updatedAt 1721282147 at that block."
    }
